  }
  [34mif[39m ([34mtypeof[39m window !== [31m"undefined"[39m) {
    window.AppSettings = [33mbuildSettings[39m(window.location.hostname);
  }

  [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m has no [38;5;153m"type"[39m field, so Node treats [38;5;153m.js[39m as CommonJS and [38;5;153mrequire("../settings.js")[39m works with no tooling.
  In the browser the [38;5;153mmodule[39m branch is skipped and behavior is exactly as described above.

  The cost is honest: seven lines of dual-mode boilerplate in a file that's otherwise a lookup table, and a
  [38;5;153mmodule[39m/[38;5;153mwindow[39m sniff that reads as dated. The alternative — splitting [38;5;153mdetectEnvironment[39m into its own file so the
  browser file stays pure — trades that for a two-file settings layer in a repo with four files. I'd take the
  boilerplate.

  So the full scope becomes:

  ┌───────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │         File          │                                     Change                                      │
  ├───────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153msettings.js[39m           │ New — environment table, [38;5;153mdetectEnvironment()[39m, [38;5;153mbuildSettings()[39m, dual export      │
  ├───────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mapp.js[39m                │ One line: read [38;5;153mwindow.AppSettings.loginEndpoint[39m; add the missing-settings guard │
  ├───────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mindex.html[39m            │ One line: [38;5;153m<script src="settings.js">[39m before [38;5;153mapp.js[39m                              │
  ├───────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mtest/settings.test.js[39m │ New — [38;5;153mnode:test[39m cases for each hostname branch and the unknown-host fallback    │
  ├───────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m          │ Add [38;5;153m"scripts": { "test": "node --test" }[39m                                        │
  └───────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Does this design look right? If yes, I'll write it up as a spec at
  [38;5;153mdocs/hyperpowers/specs/2026-09-16-settings-module-design.md[39m (uncommitted) for you to review before any code gets
  written — and I still need the real staging hostname and local API port, which I'll mark as assumptions in the spec if
  you don't have them handy.

